  "description": "NAMVOP crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P b c a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H88 N10 O32 Tb6. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1D (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2D (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3D (Tb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.549-4.019 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.17-114.43°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C78H88Tb6N10O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
